n.\n   - Use rigorous testing methods including:\n     - Unit tests for code correctness.\n     - Statistical validation for model accuracy.\n     - Stress tests simulating extreme or unexpected inputs.\n     - Adversarial testing to probe model vulnerabilities.\n   - Verify that AI outputs are consistent, justifiable, and aligned with ethical standards.\n   - Document testing procedures and outcomes for accountability.\n\n5. **Deploy with Monitoring and Feedback Loops**\n   - Establish real-time monitoring systems tracking:\n     - Performance metrics (accuracy, response time).\n     - Security anomalies or breaches.\n     - Compliance with operational constraints.\n   - Implement detailed logging for audit trails, including input data, decisions made, and actions triggered.\n   - Create feedback channels for users and stakeholders to report issues or unexpected behavior.\n   - Define clear incident response protocols to address failures swiftly.\n\n6. **Train Employees and Stakeholders**\n   - Educate relevant teams on the capabilities, limitations, and ethical considerations of AI agents.\n   - Train users on proper AI interaction and how to recognize and report problematic outputs.\n   - Foster an organizational culture emphasizing responsibility, transparency, and continuous improvement.\n\n7. **Continuous Improvement**\n   - Set up processes for ongoing model updates based on new data, user feedback, and emerging risks.\n   - Periodically reassess risks and conduct safety audits to detect drift or degradation.\n   - Stay informed on evolving regulations and industry best practices, adapting governance accordingly.\n   - Use metrics and KPIs to guide iterative improvements and justify continued deployment.\n\n**Risks to monitor and mitigate:**\n- Model bias causing discrimination or reputational harm.\n- Data breaches exposing sensitive information.\n- Overreliance on AI decisions without sufficient human oversight.\n- Regulatory non-compliance leading to legal